Package: usb4-rdma-provider
Version: @VERSION@
Section: libs
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Depends: libibverbs1, iproute2
Breaks: thunderbolt-ibverbs-dkms (<< 0.2.70)
Replaces: thunderbolt-ibverbs-dkms (<< 0.2.70)
Maintainer: AppMana <ops@appmana.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/AppMana/forks-thunderbolt
Description: ALPHA usb4_rdma and tbrxe libibverbs userspace providers
 Drop-in libibverbs providers for the AppMana Thunderbolt/USB4 RDMA engine:
 the tbrxe provider binds the thunderbolt_frame_rxe kernel devices (rxe
 uverbs ABI under the private USB4 driver id, coexisting with the distro's
 librxe); the usb4_rdma provider serves the retired legacy engine's private
 ABI and remains for archival compatibility. Install alongside the matching
 thunderbolt-frame-dkms package for full ibv_devices visibility and
 downstream RDMA tool support (NCCL, vllm, perftest). Also carries the udev
 tooling for the u4r* rail netdevs: stable per-link naming (tbr-<peer>) and
 the deterministic per-link /64 ULA assignment (tbv-rdma-addr, installed
 under /usr/lib/usb4-rdma/). This AppMana build is alpha/pre-release
 software.
